{
  "contract": "Every public booking surface must resolve its visual identity \u2014 brandColor, darkBrandColor and the light/dark theme preference \u2014 from the same entity hierarchy: the organisation that owns the entity being booked takes precedence over (or at minimum supplies the fallback for) the individual member's own appearance settings, exactly as it already does for a team's events via the team's parent organisation. Any query that feeds a public page must therefore select the organisation's branding columns, any type that carries an organisation onto a user profile must declare them, and any page or hook that applies theme/brand must take them from that resolved profile rather than from the member record alone.",
  "defect_location": {
    "repo": "calcom/cal.com",
    "summary": "The branding hierarchy is implemented only on the team path. packages/features/eventtypes/lib/getPublicEvent.ts:585-614 computes `styleProfile = team || event.parent?.team || nonTeamProfile`, so a team event inherits the parent organisation's brandColor/darkBrandColor/theme (lines 606-608), while a personal event type falls through to `nonTeamProfile` \u2014 the user \u2014 and the user's organisation is never consulted. The organisation branding is not even fetched on that path: the user select at packages/features/eventtypes/lib/getPublicEvent.ts:31-48 pulls `organization: { id, name, slug, bannerUrl }` with no brand or theme columns. The same omission repeats upstream: packages/features/users/repositories/UserRepository.ts:71-80 (`teamSelect`, used by `findUsersByUsername` at :169-179 for the personal pages) and packages/features/profile/repositories/ProfileRepository.ts:44-53 (`organizationSelect`) both stop at logoUrl/bannerUrl/hideBranding, and the shared type packages/types/UserProfile.d.ts:3-5 declares the attached organisation as Pick<Team, \"name\"|\"id\"|\"slug\"|\"calVideoLogo\"|\"bannerUrl\"> only. Consequently apps/web/server/lib/[user]/getServerSideProps.ts:133-145 builds the personal-link profile as `theme: user.theme, brandColor: user.brandColor ?? DEFAULT_LIGHT_BRAND_COLOR, darkBrandColor: user.darkBrandColor ?? DEFAULT_DARK_BRAND_COLOR`, and apps/web/modules/users/views/users-public-view.tsx:29 applies only `useTheme(profile.theme)` with no brand colours at all. The personal event-type page inherits the same wrong values because apps/web/server/lib/[user]/[type]/getServerSideProps.ts:247-282 passes the eventData straight through from packages/features/eventtypes/repositories/EventRepository.ts, and packages/platform/atoms/booker/BookerWebWrapper.tsx:203-207 feeds `event.data.profile.brandColor/darkBrandColor/theme` into packages/features/bookings/Booker/utils/use-brand-colors.tsx:5-21. By contrast apps/web/modules/team/team-view.tsx:36 uses `useTheme(team.theme)`, which is why the team links look right and the personal links do not.",
    "repo_relative_note": "all line references are at commit 9d4522825bc39621a4d6385f7c13643e64142e10"
  },
